AWS Lamda:- It is a compute service that lets you run code without having to provision or manage servers. 
	    Lamda is aws serverless offering. Aws manages the server maintainance scalling capacity provisioning and logging. 
	    Upload you code to lambda and aws has lambda service reserve service pool. 
	    So whole bunch of instances that are just kind of sitting and waiting. If certain period is going to occur. Lambda pull a couple of instances from the reserve service pool. and run your code. After all done its going to send back the instances. 
	    Its practially not the serverless, its just that Aws is managing all of the server under the hood. 

Lambda use cases:- File Proccssing, Stream Processing, Web Application, Mobile/web Backend. 

Benifits Of Lambda:- No servers to manage.
		     No Need for an infra team. 
		     No patching/upgrading
		     Faster Development
		     Auto Scale to handle traffic spikes.
		     Pay for what you use. 
		     Pay per invocation.
		     No extra cost during low traffic.

Downsides of Lambda:- No Local State.
		      Will need a seperate database to store data that needs to persist.
		      Limited execution duration. Function can run for most 15 mins. after that its timeout.
		      Not good for long running tasks.
		      It has cold start issues. Cold start occur due to the time it takes to initialize and load the function. 

Lambda Pricing:- Number of times function ran.
		 How long did it run for.
		 How much memory/cpu did it require.


